{"id":2193,"date":"2025-05-22T11:15:16","date_gmt":"2025-05-22T16:15:16","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/?post_type=news&#038;p=2193"},"modified":"2025-05-22T11:15:16","modified_gmt":"2025-05-22T16:15:16","slug":"announcing-the-twilight-magus","status":"publish","type":"news","link":"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/announcing-the-twilight-magus\/","title":{"rendered":"Announcing The Twilight Magus"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>You could be forgiven for thinking we&#8217;d seen the last of Carl Sanford. In the aftermath of <em><a href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/books\/herald-of-ruin\/\">Herald of Ruin<\/a><\/em> and the events of <em><a href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/the-drowned-city-campaign-expansion-available-now\/\">The Drowned City<\/a><\/em>, the one-time leader of the Silver Twilight Lodge was forced to depart Arkham, seemingly usurped by the ascendant Randall Tillinghast. <\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-medium\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2025\/05\/Twilight-Magus-Announced_body_01-241x300.webp\" alt=\"Oil painting of Carl Sanford, former master of the Silver Twilight Lodge\" class=\"wp-image-2195\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<p>But even in exile, Sanford lusts for power \u2013 and he has a plan to get it, in <em>The Twilight Magus<\/em>, a brand-new Arkham Horror novel by author Tim Pratt, coming this July from Aconyte Books.  <\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-medium\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2025\/05\/Twilight-Magus-Announced_body_02-212x300.webp\" alt=\"Cover of The Twilight Magus\" class=\"wp-image-2196\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<p><em>The Twilight Magus <\/em>continues the story of Sanford&#8217;s quest for occult power begun in <em>The Ravening Deep <\/em>and <em>Herald of Ruin<\/em>. This time, though, Sanford is far from home\u2026<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>From Aconyte Books:<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"lazyblock-block-quote-2qqtj4 wp-block-lazyblock-block-quote\"><blockquote class=\"text-sand-white text-left px-8 md:pl-16 py-16 space-y-4 max-w-xl mx-auto\">\n    <p><p>Carl Sanford, once the Silver Twilight Lodge\u2019s great leader and now presumed dead, lives in anonymity in Spain, plotting revenge against those who betrayed him. Alone, he calculates his first move to achieve power abroad is by being initiated into the mysterious ancient society called the Red Coterie to secretly take it over. Despite Sanford\u2019s reputation, the Red Coterie demands proof of his occult prowess, sending him on a quest to vanquish The Blood Moon, a reclusive blood magus manipulating humans and monsters alike to achieve their own ends. As Sanford uses every scrap of cunning he possesses to outwit his enemies and prove his worth, old foes from Arkham have discovered his existence and are coming to finish him off once and for all.<\/p><\/p>\n    <cite><\/cite>\n<\/blockquote><\/div>\n\n\n<p>We&#8217;ll have more on <em>The Twilight Magus<\/em>, including release date and pre-order details soon. In the meantime, sign up to the <a href=\"https:\/\/newsletter.asmodee.net\/fr\/arkhamhorror\">Arkham Horror <\/a>and <a href=\"https:\/\/www.aconytebooks.com\/aconyte-mailing-list\/\">Aconyte Books<\/a> newsletters to make sure you never miss a thing. And if you haven&#8217;t already read the beginnings of Sanford&#8217;s saga in <em><a href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/books\/the-ravening-deep\/\">The Ravening Deep<\/a> <\/em>and <em><a href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/books\/herald-of-ruin\/\">Herald of Ruin<\/a> <\/em>now would be a great time to catch up. <\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/image-converter?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.svc.asmodee.net%2Fproduction-arkhamhorror%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FTwilight-Magus-Announced_body_03-1024x539.jpg&amp;attachment_id=2197\" alt=\"The Carl Sanford trilogy: The Ravening Deep, Herald of Ruin and The Twilight Magus\" class=\"wp-image-2197\"\/><\/figure><\/div>","protected":false},"featured_media":2198,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":true},"key-tag":[34,17,32],"class_list":["post-2193","news","type-news","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","key-tag-aconyte","key-tag-books","key-tag-novels"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO Premium plugin v22.3 (Yoast SEO v22.9) - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>Announcing The Twilight Magus | ArkhamHorror.com | The Official Arkham Horror Website News<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"The Twilight Magus continues the story of Sanford&#039;s quest for occult power begun in The Ravening Deep and Herald of Ruin.\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/announcing-the-twilight-magus\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Announcing The Twilight Magus | ArkhamHorror.com | The Official Arkham Horror Website News\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"The Twilight Magus continues the story of Sanford&#039;s quest for occult power begun in The Ravening Deep and Herald of Ruin.\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/announcing-the-twilight-magus\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"ArkhamHorror.com | The Official Arkham Horror Website\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/ArkhamHorrorOfficial\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.c